From 09730f58b3d810b2331215c7645454d60f0fcf99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed Yasser <midogamer100@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:57:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Integration API: statement-v2 dataset with per-entry
 content digest

- Manifest computes entries_sha256 (SHA-256 over the canonical encoding of every
  entry of the period) in the same REPEATABLE READ snapshot; dataset_id covers it.
- Entries expose posted_at_us (integer microseconds) used by the digest.
- NVB_INTEGRATION_MAX_STATEMENT_ENTRIES bounds the rows hashed per manifest
  (422 dataset_too_large instead of truncation).
- Tests: back-dated rows, in-place edits and delete/re-insert with identical
  count/totals are detected; PostgreSQL-only snapshot/read-only/concurrency tests.
- Fix test_integration_disabled_by_default so it also runs on PostgreSQL.

No schema change, no migration. Still disabled by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
